      "endSeconds": 11.475,
      "index": 0,
      "sceneId": "title",
      "startSeconds": 0.25,
      "text": "Bottom line: Copilot Autopilot is a bounded standing role, not a chatbot. Pilot privately with one owner, scoped access, cost guardrail and review."
    },
    {
      "endSeconds": 27.2,
      "index": 1,
      "sceneId": "operating-model",
      "startSeconds": 12.025,
      "text": "The shift is from asking for an answer to assigning a standing role. Autopilot brings identity, memory and a workspace; leaders still own objectives and boundaries. Governance changes with the unit of delegation."
    },
    {
      "endSeconds": 43.8,
      "index": 2,
      "sceneId": "identity-boundaries",
      "startSeconds": 27.75,
      "text": "Foundry is an architectural lens, not proof of identical implementation. Identity anchors the standing role; the organization still bounds interactions, access and actions, with a manager accountable for the role."
    },
    {
      "endSeconds": 61.025,
      "index": 3,
      "sceneId": "pilot",
      "startSeconds": 44.35,
      "text": "Pilot one recurring workflow with one team and owner. Reuse blueprint logic, but scope each instance to its own permissions and assignment. While Autopilot is private preview, require a stop condition and review before expansion."
    }
  ],
